        heading: "Indoor Farm Dehumidification Design Checklist",
        body: "Use this checklist before dehumidification equipment is selected:\n\n• Peak moisture load established with the room's temperature and humidity targets plotted on the psychrometric chart\n• Coil dew point and reheat strategy designed explicitly — never assumed from comfort cooling equipment\n• Technology selected for the temperature regime: DX, desiccant, or integrated reheat, compared on efficiency at real conditions\n• Equipment capacity verified at the room's actual day, night, and part-load conditions, not the catalog rating point\n• Rejected heat mapped to useful sinks or carried explicitly in the cooling load\n• Condensate collection sized for the peak removal hour, piped to drain or captured for reuse with proper trapping\n• Staging controls sequenced to the daily load curve with smooth capacity tracking and no short-cycling\n• Redundancy evaluated for sealed rooms against crop value, with N+1 capacity priced as an option",
