        heading: "Indoor Crop Lighting Design Checklist",
        body: "Use this checklist before the crop lighting design is finalized:\n\n• Fixtures compared on micromoles per joule at realistic operating temperatures, with total cost of ownership modeled\n• Heat rejected per photon carried into the cooling load — efficacy evaluated on photons and cooling together\n• Layout verified for uniformity at real mounting heights so no energy is wasted on over-lit hotspots\n• Photoperiod schedule modeled against the site's actual utility tariff: time-of-use, demand charges, available ag rates\n• Zone startup staging designed so the farm never peaks the electrical service, including after power restoration\n• DLI-based dimming specified with demand capping during the utility's peak window\n• Depreciation headroom in the initial light level, with a cleaning schedule and periodic PPFD verification planned\n• Fixture replacement budgeted by operating hours with accessible mounting for cleaning and service",
