        question: "What does micromoles per joule actually tell you?",
        answer: "How many usable photons a fixture produces per unit of electricity — the fundamental efficiency of the light as a growing tool. Higher efficacy means more crop-driving light per dollar of power and less waste heat per photon, which also shrinks the cooling load. The engineer compares fixtures on this number at realistic temperatures and uses it as the basis for the total-cost-of-ownership model, not just the purchase price.",
