        body: "Use this checklist before the mushroom facility design is finalized:\n\n• Climate recipes documented per growth stage: spawn run, pinning, and fruiting temperature, humidity, and air exchange\n• Humidification sized to hold 85 to 95 percent RH through the design-day fresh-air load, zoned per room\n• All room construction corrosion-proof and mold-resistant: sealed electrical, sloped floors to drains, sealed penetrations\n• Fresh-air exchange rate calculated from peak crop CO2 production, with filtered, tempered incoming air\n• Steam or heat capacity provided for substrate pasteurization with condensate handling\n• One-way process flow from substrate prep through fruiting, with airlocks or pressure cascades at zone boundaries\n• Washdown provisions designed: hot water, hose stations, chemical-resistant finishes, and chemical storage containment\n• Exhaust placement checked against intakes, neighboring properties, and any local odor or nuisance requirements",
