        heading: "Aquaponics System Design Checklist",
        body: "Use this checklist before the aquaponics design is finalized:\n\n• Fish stocking, species, and feeding rates documented as the basis for all waste-load calculations\n• Biofilter sized from ammonia production at operating temperature with safety factors for colony disruption\n• Solids separation placed before the biofilter and sized to peak feeding loads, with an approved solids handling path\n• Plant growing area matched to the fish side's steady-state nutrient output so nitrate stays in the healthy band\n• Dissolved oxygen, pH, temperature, and ammonia monitored continuously with trending and escalating alarms\n• Aeration and circulation on automatic backup power with autonomy sized to local outage history\n• Redundancy provided for the fastest-killing failure modes: aeration, circulation, and temperature control\n• Isolation valves and bypasses detailed so any component can be serviced without draining the fish system",
