        question: "How do fish and plants share one water loop safely?",
        answer: "Through bacteria in the middle. Fish excrete ammonia, which is toxic to them; nitrifying bacteria in the biofilter convert ammonia to nitrite then nitrate; plants absorb the nitrate as fertilizer, cleaning the water that returns to the fish. The engineer sizes each stage — fish load, biofilter capacity, plant uptake area — so the conversions keep pace and no intermediate compound accumulates to dangerous levels.",
