        body: "The load calculation is built tier by tier. The engineer totals the dead load of the rack steel, the growing system hardware, the water or nutrient solution at full operating level, the mature plant mass, and the lighting fixtures — then adds the live loads of workers accessing the tiers and the dynamic effects of harvest activity. Connections get the same rigor as the members: a rack is only as strong as its bolted or welded joints, and the engineer specifies the connection design rather than accepting catalog capacity at face value for the loaded heights involved.\n\nStability analysis covers the modes catalog racks ignore. The engineer checks overturning of tall narrow rows, the bracing system's capacity in both directions, and the anchorage for combined shear and uplift under seismic loading per the code. Where racks exceed the heights or configurations the manufacturer's certification covers, the engineer designs the supplemental bracing and anchorage explicitly. Floor anchorage is detailed with the slab capacity in mind — post-tensioned slabs, thin slabs, and slabs with unknown capacity each get their own treatment — and the engineer verifies the anchors against the actual floor, not an assumed one.",
